Article 3 The limitation of action for the issuing bank's rights claim against the cardholder shall be deemed interrupted under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The issuing bank deducts the principal and interest of overdraft, liquidated damages, etc. from the cardholder's account as agreed;
(2) The issuing bank collects the claim by sending SMS messages, written letters, emails, etc. to the cardholder's reserved telephone number, correspondence address, or email address;
(3) The issuing bank reports to the public security organ on the ground that the cardholder's malicious overdraft is suspected of constituting a crime;
(4) Other circumstances that may be deemed as interruption of limitation of action.
